<section image-layout="blank" id="2c8VJsD1TL" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.42" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/y51aL5DS_jH1dld2ID2jD.png" saved-media-id="qoj0v6qbppcfehj" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast editorial studio photograph of a near-black doorway standing slightly open on the right, a narrow bone-white rectangle of practical hard light crossing the floor, one amber long-exposure line passing through the opening and leaving a faint ultraviolet residual trace, deep uncluttered negative space on the left, restrained film grain, no people, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"/><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7SmFbo4AlK" vertical-align="end" colspan="31"><p role="eyebrow">Protect the promise. Loosen the route.</p><display size="lg">Leave a door<br/><span text-color="accent">open</span></display><p font-size="lg">Name the promise. Fix one constraint. Change one variable. Keep only what earns its place.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"/><h3 role="subheading">Rigor does not eliminate the unexpected. It creates a way to recognize it.</h3></grid-item><spacer span="29"></spacer></grid></section>